<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-10-16T19:08:52+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Fri, 16 Oct 2026 19:08:52 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[UN warns Russian attacks and winter hardship could displace more Ukrainians]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134996472.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[As winter approaches, Ukraine faces dire challenges with essential services declining due to ongoing conflict. Millions of internally displaced individuals struggle to reunite with their homes, often in ruins. With falling temperatures, access to heating, electricity, and safe drinking water becomes precarious. Funding shortages jeopardize relief initiatives, leaving countless families at risk. Humanitarian organizations are ramping up efforts to offer vital support to affected communities.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/un-warns-russian-attacks-and-winter-hardship-could-displace-more-ukrainians/articleshow/134996472.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/un-warns-russian-attacks-and-winter-hardship-could-displace-more-ukrainians/articleshow/134996472.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-16T18:58:43+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Mahima Sharma</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134996587,imgsize-211119.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Judge upholds solar deal on 562.8 acres, keeping $330M project in play]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134995018.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2020-members-of-a-michigan-farming-family-signed-solar-option-agreements-covering-562-8-acres-a-judge-has-now-ruled-them-valid-keeping-nearly-30-of-a-proposed-330-million-solar-project-in-play/articleshow/134995018.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2020-members-of-a-michigan-farming-family-signed-solar-option-agreements-covering-562-8-acres-a-judge-has-now-ruled-them-valid-keeping-nearly-30-of-a-proposed-330-million-solar-project-in-play/articleshow/134995018.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-16T19:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134995203,imgsize-853610.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Michigan Court Upholds 2012 Survivorship Deed, Rejects Daughter’s Claim to Troy Home]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134993244.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Michigan appeals court has confirmed the validity of a survivorship deed that granted ownership of a house to Jessica Rae Harless. The ruling asserts that Shirley Ann Page's 2012 deed established a joint tenancy with rights of survivorship. Despite Anita Lanctot's challenge regarding the absence of the term 'joint' in the deed, the court affirmed that Page's intent was unmistakably conveyed, ensuring Harless retains sole ownership of the property.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2012-a-michigan-woman-put-her-troy-home-in-her-name-and-that-of-a-woman-who-regarded-her-as-a-grandmother-14-years-later-an-appeals-court-upheld-the-survivorship-deed-over-her-daughters-challenge/articleshow/134993244.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2012-a-michigan-woman-put-her-troy-home-in-her-name-and-that-of-a-woman-who-regarded-her-as-a-grandmother-14-years-later-an-appeals-court-upheld-the-survivorship-deed-over-her-daughters-challenge/articleshow/134993244.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-16T18:25:56+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134995883,imgsize-1679145.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[China asks Katie Zacharia to visit more often as press secretary says China did not have proper toilets]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134995706.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/china-asks-katie-zacharia-to-visit-more-often-as-press-secretary-says-china-did-not-have-proper-toilets/articleshow/134995706.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/china-asks-katie-zacharia-to-visit-more-often-as-press-secretary-says-china-did-not-have-proper-toilets/articleshow/134995706.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-16T18:22:01+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="h