 World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134995154,imgsize-1573644.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Georgia renter warned landlord about tree; after it crushed his home, appeals court revived claims]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134994470.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[William Frank Jennings, a Lindale, Georgia resident, became paralyzed after a tree fell on his house, despite having warned his landlord about its dangerous state. The Georgia Court of Appeals ruled that his claims against Romulus Investments were improperly dismissed, noting significant conflicting evidence regarding hazard notifications. This ruling enables Jennings to pursue his case further to potentially establish liability and seek damages for his injuries.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/georgia-renter-warned-his-landlord-about-an-80-year-old-tree-next-door-after-branches-hit-his-home-and-truck-when-it-later-crushed-the-house-and-left-him-paralysed-an-appeals-court-revived-his-claims/articleshow/134994470.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/georgia-renter-warned-his-landlord-about-an-80-year-old-tree-next-door-after-branches-hit-his-home-and-truck-when-it-later-crushed-the-house-and-left-him-paralysed-an-appeals-court-revived-his-claims/articleshow/134994470.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-16T17:59:26+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134994619,imgsize-2272001.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[John Griffin sells Regent’s Park mansion at £9.2m loss]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134990225.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[John Griffin, the mind behind Addison Lee, experienced a substantial loss after selling his lavish London mansion for £11.5 million, down from the £20.7 million he paid in 2013, incurring a staggering loss of £9.2 million. This sale reflects the broader downturn in London's property landscape, impacted by economic instability and new tax regulations.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-2013-addison-lee-founder-john-griffin-paid-20-7-million-for-a-regents-park-mansion-and-later-asked-32-million-13-years-later-the-six-bedroom-home-has-sold-for-11-5-million/articleshow/134990225.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-2013-addison-lee-founder-john-griffin-paid-20-7-million-for-a-regents-park-mansion-and-later-asked-32-million-13-years-later-the-six-bedroom-home-has-sold-for-11-5-million/articleshow/134990225.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-16T17:59:08+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134990288,imgsize-225446.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Henry Nowak murder case: Sikh man's mother may be released early under new UK prison rules]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134994706.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/henry-nowak-murder-case-sikh-mans-mother-may-be-released-early-under-new-uk-prison-rules/articleshow/134994706.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/henry-nowak-murder-case-sikh-mans-mother-may-be-released-early-under-new-uk-prison-rules/articleshow/134994706.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-16T17:52:06+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Gokul Ankari</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134994963,imgsize-1127148.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[75,000-year-old Neanderthal remains reveal possible fatal spear attack and signs of care]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134991338.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Neanderthal who lived 75,000 years ago survived a severe facial injury for at least a year before suffering a possibly fatal spear wound. Researchers studying remains found in Iraq’s Shanidar Cave identified a 15mm hole in the shoulder blade, suggesting a wooden spear injury. The findings also point to possible care from other Neanderthals.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/a-neanderthal-survived-a-severe-facial-injury-for-at-least-a-year-before-dying-75000-years-ago-a-15mm-shoulder-blade-hole-may-be-the-earliest-evidence-of-lethal-violence-with-a-wooden-spear/articleshow/134991338.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/a-neanderthal-survived-a-severe-facial-injury-for-at-least-a-year-before-dying-75000-years-ago-a-15mm-shoulder-blade-hole-may-be-the-earliest-evidence-of-lethal-violence-with-a-wooden-spear/articleshow/134991338.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-16T17:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134992127,imgsize-73742.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Katie Zacharia admits she failed the bar exam on her first attempt in 2011, years after calling herself a lawyer]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134994490.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/katie-zacharia-admits-she-failed-the-bar-exam-on-her-first-attempt-in-2011-years-after-calling-herself-a-lawyer/articleshow/134994490.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/katie-zacharia-admits-she-failed-the-bar-exam-on-her-first-attempt-in-2011-years-after-calling-herself-a-lawyer/articleshow/134994490.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-16T17:35:44+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134994544,imgsize-120632.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[California court rules rental income cannot reduce siblings’ inheritance shares]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134994195.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/five-siblings-fought-over-their-late-mothers-trust-and-property-income-california-court-rules-rental-proceeds-cannot-reduce-inheritance-shares/articleshow/134994195.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/five-siblings-fought-over-their-late-mothers-trust-and-property-income-california-court-rules-rental-proceeds-cannot-reduce-inheritance-shares/articleshow/134994195.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-16T17:27:21+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134994286,imgsize-108504.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[16-year-old collected 60 backpacks for 7 schools, then created 4 ‘Kindness Karts’]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134993507.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/16-year-old-pennsylvania-student-collected-60-backpacks-filled-with-supplies-and-hundreds-of-stationery-items-then-distributed-them-across-seven-schools-and-created-four-kindness-karts-to-encourage-students-to-pay-kindness-forward/articleshow/134993507.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/16-year-old-pennsylvania-student-collected-60-backpacks-filled-with-supplies-and-hundreds-of-stationery-items-then-distributed-them-across-seven-schools-and-created-four-kindness-karts-to-encourage-students-to-pay-kindness-forward/articleshow/134993507.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-16T17:14:59+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134993597,imgsize-1250299.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Can't replace capability': Starlink disruption exposes Ukraine's reliance on US tech]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134992436.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[EU leaders are addressing concerns regarding Ukraine's reliance on Elon Musk's Starlink satellite for military communications. Disruptions to the Starlink service have highlighted the urgent need for European alternatives. Officials discussed how to strengthen Europe's satellite communication capabilities during a recent summit with Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy. Investor interest in European satellite companies, such as Eutelsat and SES, has surged after the disruptions.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/starlink-disruption-exposes-ukraines-reliance-on-us-tech-europe-admits-cant-replace-capability/articleshow/134992436.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/starlink-disruption-exposes-ukraines-reliance-on-us-tech-europe-admits-cant-replace-capability/articleshow/134992436.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-16T16:46:41+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134992921,imgsize-917195.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Pakistan to chair IMF, World Bank boards in 2027; first time in over 70 years]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134993350.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Pakistan will assume the chairmanship of the IMF and World Bank Group boards in 2027, marking a significant return. This follows a long absence from the position that last occurred in 1953. The role will allow Pakistan to engage in global economic discussions and foster collaboration among member nations. Pakistan is currently utilizing financial assistance from the IMF through various programs aimed at economic stabilization.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/pakistan/pakistan-to-chair-imf-world-bank-boards-in-2027-first-time-in-over-70-years-/articleshow/134993350.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/pakistan/pakistan-to-chair-imf-world-bank-boards-in-2027-first-time-in-over-70-years-/articleshow/134993350.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-16T17:06:24+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pranjal Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134993530,imgsize-84924.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Rare 1953 James Bond book bought for £1 at car boot sale sells for £10,000]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134991543.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A woman bought a book at a car boot sale in Yorkshire for just £1 ten years ago. She later discovered it was a rare first edition of Casino Royale by Ian Fleming. The book retained its original dust jacket and was valued significantly. It was auctioned for £10,000, highlighting the importance of rarity and condition in collectibles. The successful bidder was a UK collector specializing in Ian Fleming editions.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-shopper-paid-just-1-at-a-uk-car-boot-sale-for-a-1953-first-edition-casino-royale-in-its-original-dust-jacket-after-experts-recognised-the-rare-james-bond-book-it-sold-at-auction-for-10000/articleshow/134991543.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-shopper-paid-just-1-at-a-uk-car-boot-sale-for-a-1953-first-edition-casino-royale-in-its-original-dust-jacket-after-experts-recognised-the-rare-james-bond-book-it-sold-at-auction-for-10000/articleshow/134991543.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-16T17:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134991961,imgsize-62590.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Arizona teen gave a stranger his shoes, learnt he lost his wife, raised $25,000]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134992501.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-arizona-teen-gave-an-elderly-stranger-his-shoes-learnt-he-had-lost-his-wife-then-launched-a-gofundme-that-raised-25000/articleshow/134992501.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-arizona-teen-gave-an-elderly-stranger-his-shoes-learnt-he-had-lost-his-wife-then-launched-a-gofundme-that-raised-25000/articleshow/134992501.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-16T16:43:18+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134992750,imgsize-1795466.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Black ink on Tagore: The fight over Bangladesh's identity]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134990572.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The recent defacement of Rabindranath Tagore's portrait in Dhaka has stirred a fresh wave of conversations about his legacy. Against the backdrop of increased political unease post the July 2024 uprising and claims against Jamaat-e-Islami, public outcry highlights the threat to cultural icons. This event has mobilized protests and reinvigorated discussions, reflecting on the vital intersection of politics, culture, and the essence of national identity in contemporary Bangladesh.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/black-ink-on-tagore-the-fight-over-bangladeshs-identity/articleshow/134990572.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/black-ink-on-tagore-the-fight-over-bangladeshs-identity/articleshow/134990572.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-16T15:54:57+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Arghya Prasun Roychowdhury</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134990843,imgsize-53436.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[9 ex-FBI employees sue Trump admin over Mar-a-Lago probe, claim political retaliation]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134992004.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/9-ex-fbi-employees-sue-trump-admin-over-mar-a-lago-probe-claim-political-retaliation/articleshow/134992004.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/9-ex-fbi-employees-sue-trump-admin-over-mar-a-lago-probe-claim-political-retaliation/articleshow/134992004.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10